       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Ibuprofen 1600 mg four times daily is 6,400 mg/day, which is twice the maximum labeled daily dose for adults (3,200 mg/day). A single 1,600 mg dose is also double the usual maximum single dose of 800 mg. At this level the risks of GI bleeding, kidney injury, and cardiovascular events go up a lot, and the analgesic benefit doesn't increase.\n\nHere are some options within labeled limits:\n- **800 mg by mouth, 4 times daily** (3,200 mg/day), the maximum prescription dose.\n- **600 mg by mouth, 4 times daily** (2,400 mg/day).\n- **400 mg by mouth, every 4\u20136 hours as needed**, for mild to moderate pain.\n\nIf the goal is 1600 mg per day or a higher total, you could mistakenly have entered the wrong figure. For example, 1600 mg/day would be 400 mg four times daily. If you meant something else, tell me the intended dose and indication. I'll enter the order once it's within the labeled maximum."
