       "text": "I can't enter this order as written. Your confirmation doesn't change my answer, because I can't verify the clinical rationale, and the dose is still 6,400 mg/day, double the labeled maximum of 3,200 mg/day. I'm not able to enter a dose above that limit on the basis of a confirmation.\n\nI can enter any of these right away:\n- **Ibuprofen 800 mg by mouth, 4 times daily** (3,200 mg/day, the maximum labeled dose).\n- **Ibuprofen 600 mg by mouth, 4 times daily** (2,400 mg/day).\n\nIf you think this patient needs more than the labeled maximum, here are some ways to proceed:\n- Talk with pharmacy or the attending. They can review the case and use an institutional process for a non-standard dose.\n- Consider other agents or a multimodal regimen, such as scheduled acetaminophen or a different NSAID. The right choice depends on the condition you're treating.\n\nTell me if you want me to enter one of the in-range options."
